--- D1: the psi equation and the single-stream Bernoulli identity ---
D1 PASS psi-eq residual 0; Bernoulli residuals [0, 0, 0] all 0  lap psi = 4piG rho_b - div[mu grad Xi] - muK^2 Xi ; Dv/Dt = -grad(Phi - Xi) for v = -grad sigma

--- D2: literal statics (uniqueness at muK = 0; zero-point freedom at muK != 0) ---
D2 PASS Eq35 residual 0; d(x mu)/dx = x*(x + 2)/(x**2 + 2*x + 1) > 0, d(x(1-mu))/dx = 1/(x**2 + 2*x + 1) > 0; K-dust shift residual 0; Helmholtz mode residual 0 residuals 0, fluxes increasing  static LIT: Xi = Phi + C => BS24 Eq.35 (unique at muK=0); muK != 0: C shifts uniform K-dust by -muK^2 C/4piG, regular sin(muK r)/r mode

--- D3: the hold cap ---
D3 PASS lim x(1-mu) = 1; 1 - x(1-mu) = 1/(x + 1) > 0; phantom-flux identity residual 0 lim 1, gap > 0, residual 0  G M_tau(V) < a0 |dV|/4pi ; sphere G M_tau(<r) < a0 r^2 ; sheet Sigma_tau < a0/2piG ; spherical g < g_N + a0

--- D4: spherical dust force and the sign of the held dust's self-interaction ---
D4 FAIL psi' form residual -m/(m - 1); AQUAL residual 0; psi'(m_ph) 0; d(psi')/dm = 1 (max 1.000e+00) residuals 0; d/dm <= 0  -psi' = -a0[n - m^2/(1-m)]; held dust self-repulsive for m > 0, neutral at m -> 0 (D-T)

--- D5: geometry-free virial: W_self >= 0 ---
D5 PASS Derrick residual 0; f(u) series 12*u**5/5 - 7*u**4/4 + u**3; f/u -> 2; min f on grid 1.000e-24 residual 0; min f >= -1e-12  W_self = W_N + (1/4piG) Int[3 Lambda - A y^2] >= (a0^2/4piG) Int f(u) >= 0 (Thomson)

--- D6: linear response in a uniform host field ---
D6 PASS cold 0; hot 0; stream 0; BSK1 M4 k>>mu 0; 0<f_theta<1 on x_e grid True (max f 0.999999) residuals 0, f in (0,1)  c_theta >= 0 for k^2 >= muK^2/f; cold = EFE phantom; hot isotropic = phantom x kD^2/(k^2+kD^2); stream pole at omega_p

--- D7 (T3): held dust is weightless in a static host ---
D7 FAIL grad psi_host = 0; stress-tensor force - qE = 0; a_CM - g Mb/(Mb+Mtau) = M_tau*g/(M_b + M_tau) all 0  T3: host exerts no force on held dust; a bound unit falls at a = g M_b/(M_b + M_tau)

